<h2>4. End-to-End Walkthrough: 4 Real-World Scenarios</h2>

<div class="card">
  <h4>Scenario 1: Normal Employee Accessing Internal Application</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Input</strong>: <code>packet_size = 520 B</code>, <code>request_rate = 6.0 req/s</code>, <code>connection_count = 3.0</code>, <code>inter_arrival_time = 0.180 s</code></li>
    <li><strong>M1 Transport</strong>: Client negotiates ML-KEM-768 / ML-DSA-65 session.</li>
    <li><strong>M2 Proxy</strong>: Intercepts <code>GET /dashboard</code> on port 8443.</li>
    <li><strong>M3 Telemetry</strong>: eBPF measures standard HTTP header packet size and steady human pacing.</li>
    <li><strong>M4 Vector</strong>: <code>x = [520.0, 6.0, 3.0, 0.180]</code></li>
    <li><strong>Isolation Forest</strong>: Traverses deep tree path (Depth ~11.2). Raw score: <code>+0.1546</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Percentile Risk</strong>: Position 784 / 11,200 $\rightarrow$ <strong>Risk Score = 0.070</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Policy Gate</strong>: <code>0.070 &lt; 0.970</code> $\rightarrow$ <strong>ALLOW</strong>. Injects <code>X-Spectra-Verified: true</code>, forwards to backend:9000. HTTP 200 OK returned.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card card-warning">
  <h4>Scenario 2: Employee Unusually Rapid Activity (Moderate Anomaly)</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Input</strong>: <code>packet_size = 523 B</code>, <code>request_rate = 8.4 req/s</code>, <code>connection_count = 4.8</code>, <code>inter_arrival_time = 0.143 s</code></li>
    <li><strong>M1 Transport</strong>: Valid quantum-safe session established.</li>
    <li><strong>M2 Proxy</strong>: User clicks rapidly or an automated browser tab reloader executes.</li>
    <li><strong>M3 Telemetry</strong>: eBPF detects inter-arrival intervals shortening and frequency rising above normal human baseline.</li>
    <li><strong>M4 Vector</strong>: <code>x = [523.0, 8.4, 4.8, 0.143]</code></li>
    <li><strong>Isolation Forest</strong>: Tree paths shorten (Depth ~7.8). Raw score: <code>-0.0150</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Percentile Risk</strong>: Position 10,976 / 11,200 $\rightarrow$ <strong>Risk Score = 0.980</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Policy Gate</strong>: <code>0.970 ≤ 0.980 &lt; 0.995</code> $\rightarrow$ <strong>MFA / MONITOR</strong>. Proxy holds session and issues WebAuthn/TOTP challenge.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card card-danger">
  <h4>Scenario 3: Attacker Making Rapid Probing Connections (Reconnaissance)</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Input</strong>: <code>packet_size = 64 B</code>, <code>request_rate = 45.0 req/s</code>, <code>connection_count = 38.0</code>, <code>inter_arrival_time = 0.022 s</code></li>
    <li><strong>M1 Transport</strong>: Client opens multiple concurrent TLS handshakes.</li>
    <li><strong>M2 Proxy</strong>: Receives rapid connection attempts targeting varied microservice endpoints.</li>
    <li><strong>M3 Telemetry</strong>: eBPF socket map detects spike in concurrent sockets (<code>ct_srv_src=38</code>) and minimal packet sizes.</li>
    <li><strong>M4 Vector</strong>: <code>x = [64.0, 45.0, 38.0, 0.022]</code></li>
    <li><strong>Isolation Forest</strong>: Trees isolate observation quickly (Depth ~4.2). Raw score: <code>-0.1680</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Percentile Risk</strong>: Position 11,180 / 11,200 $\rightarrow$ <strong>Risk Score = 0.998</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Policy Gate</strong>: <code>0.998 ≥ 0.995</code> $\rightarrow$ <strong>DROP</strong>. M2 severs TCP socket immediately. Returns HTTP 403 Forbidden.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<div class="card card-danger">
  <h4>Scenario 4: Volumetric Attack / Buffer Exploit (Obvious Malicious Attack)</h4>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Input</strong>: <code>packet_size = 9500 B</code>, <code>request_rate = 300.0 req/s</code>, <code>connection_count = 80.0</code>, <code>inter_arrival_time = 0.002 s</code></li>
    <li><strong>M1 Transport</strong>: Massive inbound packet burst saturates buffer.</li>
    <li><strong>M2 Proxy</strong>: High socket contention on edge port 8443.</li>
    <li><strong>M3 Telemetry</strong>: eBPF detects maximum-MTU packet bursts and zero inter-arrival pauses (continuous saturation).</li>
    <li><strong>M4 Vector</strong>: <code>x = [9500.0, 300.0, 80.0, 0.002]</code></li>
    <li><strong>Isolation Forest</strong>: Trees isolate observation on the first or second split (Depth ~2.1). Raw score: <code>-0.2144</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Percentile Risk</strong>: Anomaly score exceeds maximum reference calibration score $\rightarrow$ <strong>Risk Score = 1.000</strong>.</li>
    <li><strong>Policy Gate</strong>: <code>1.000 ≥ 0.995</code> $\rightarrow$ <strong>DROP</strong>. Immediate TCP RST packet transmitted. IP temporarily blacklisted.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

