<h2>5. Official UNSW-NB15 Benchmark Evaluation</h2>

<p>Evaluated on the official UNSW-NB15 test set containing <strong>82,332 test samples</strong> (37,000 normal, 45,332 real attack flows):</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Metric</th>
      <th>Measured Result</th>
      <th>Engineering &amp; Academic Explanation</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Precision</strong></td>
      <td><strong>83.12%</strong> (<code>0.8312</code>)</td>
      <td>High alert reliability: When M4 raises an alarm ($\text{Risk} \ge 0.970$), it is an actual attack ~83% of the time.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Recall</strong></td>
      <td><strong>17.78%</strong> (<code>0.1778</code>)</td>
      <td>Catches 8,060 out of 45,332 attacks. Lower recall is expected because 4 flow features cannot detect single-packet stealth exploits.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>F1-Score</strong></td>
      <td><strong>29.29%</strong> (<code>0.2929</code>)</td>
      <td>Harmonic mean balancing precision and recall ($2 \cdot P \cdot R / (P + R)$); pulled down by the prototype's lower recall.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>False-Positive Rate</strong></td>
      <td><strong>4.42%</strong> (<code>0.0442</code>)</td>
      <td>Out of 37,000 normal test flows, only 1,637 triggered challenges, closely matching the theoretical ~3% design target.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>ROC-AUC</strong></td>
      <td><strong>0.7570</strong></td>
      <td>Strong continuous ranking capability across all potential decision thresholds.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Median Latency</strong></td>
      <td><strong>5.720 ms</strong></td>
      <td>Single-pass inference per request, well under enterprise proxy SLA limits.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>P95 Latency</strong></td>
      <td><strong>8.439 ms</strong></td>
      <td>95% of all inferences complete within 8.5 ms.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h3>Confusion Matrix (N = 82,332)</h3>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th></th>
      <th>Predicted Normal (Risk &lt; 0.970)</th>
      <th>Predicted Attack (Risk ≥ 0.970)</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <th>Actual Normal (37,000)</th>
      <td><strong>TN: 35,363</strong> (95.58%)</td>
      <td><strong>FP: 1,637</strong> (4.42%)</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <th>Actual Attack (45,332)</th>
      <td><strong>FN: 37,272</strong> (82.22%)</td>
      <td><strong>TP: 8,060</strong> (17.78%)</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

