<h2>8. One-Page Quick Revision Cheat Sheet</h2>

<pre><code>====================================================================================================
                              SPECTRA PROJECT CHEAT SHEET (VIVA REVISION)
====================================================================================================

PROJECT TITLE:
SPECTRA – AI-Driven PQC Reverse Proxy for Zero-Trust

CORE PURPOSE:
A Zero-Trust reverse proxy sitting in front of internal microservices that stops post-quantum 
decryption at the transport layer (M1) and prevents lateral movement at the edge via continuous 
AI behavioral telemetry risk scoring (M4).

THE 4 MODULES:
• M1 (Adaptive PQC Transport): NIST FIPS 203 (ML-KEM) & FIPS 204 (ML-DSA) via liboqs (C/C++).
  Adaptive parameter sets downshift based on client compute (Level 5 / Level 3 / Level 1).
• M2 (Zero-Trust Proxy Engine): Go reverse proxy intercepting edge traffic on 8443, forwarding to 
  internal backend 9000. Re-verifies every request. Enforces ALLOW / CHALLENGE / DROP.
• M3 (IDS & Telemetry Extraction): Kernel-level eBPF probes capturing flow metadata with zero copy; 
  Suricata deep-packet inspection for CVE signatures.
• M4 (AI Risk Engine): Unsupervised Isolation Forest evaluating 4 flow features, calibrated via 
  empirical normal percentiles to output low-latency risk scores in [0.0, 1.0].

M4 FEATURES (4 Network-Flow Dimensions):
1. packet_size (UNSW: smean)          -> Mean bytes per packet transmitted by source.
2. request_rate (UNSW: rate)          -> Transmission rate in requests/packets per second.
3. connection_count (UNSW: ct_srv_src)-> Concurrent active sockets to same service.
4. inter_arrival_time (UNSW: sinpkt)  -> Time elapsed between consecutive packets (sinpkt / 1000s).

ISOLATION FOREST MECHANICS:
• Unsupervised ensemble of 100 random decision trees.
• Core principle: "Anomalies are few and different." Outliers are isolated near the root (short depth).
• Trained strictly on NORMAL traffic (label == 0). Never sees attack labels during training.

EMPIRICAL PERCENTILE CALIBRATION:
• Normal training data split into: 80% Fit (44,800 rows) and 20% Held-Out Calibration (11,200 rows).
• Raw score = -decision_function(x).
• Risk score = empirical rank in held-out normal calibration array: risk = rank / 11,200 in [0.0, 1.0].
• Interpretation: "0.970 = more anomalous than 97.0% of held-out normal traffic."

ZERO-TRUST POLICY THRESHOLDS:
• Risk < 0.970              -> ALLOW (normal access, injects X-Spectra-Verified header).
• 0.970 <= Risk < 0.995     -> MFA / MONITOR (challenges user with step-up verification).
• Risk >= 0.995             -> DROP (top 0.5% extreme anomaly; severs TCP connection with HTTP 403).

OFFICIAL UNSW-NB15 BENCHMARK EVALUATION (82,332 Test Samples):
• Normal test samples : 37,000      • Attack test samples : 45,332
• Precision           : 83.12%      • False Positive Rate : 4.42%
• Recall              : 17.78%      • ROC-AUC             : 0.7570
• F1-Score            : 29.29%      • Latency (Median/P95): 5.720 ms / 8.439 ms
• Confusion Matrix    : TN = 35,363 | FP = 1,637 | FN = 37,272 | TP = 8,060

ATTACK CATEGORY RECALL BREAKDOWN:
• Generic: 37.78%  • Fuzzers: 8.43%  • Backdoors: 5.32%  • Analysis: 4.87%  • Worms: 4.55%
• Shellcode: 4.50% • DoS: 2.74%      • Recon: 1.60%      • Exploits: 1.52%

KEY TAKEAWAY ON RESULTS:
• High precision (83.12%) and low FPR (4.42%) prove the reliability of percentile calibration.
• Low recall (17.78%) is honest: single-packet stealth exploits mimic flow headers. This empirically
  justifies Phase 2's cross-layer fusion with Suricata IDS signatures and identity context.

STATUS DISTINCTIONS (NEVER CLAIM PLANNED AS IMPLEMENTED):
• IMPLEMENTED : Standalone M1 PQC, Standalone M2 Go proxy, Standalone M3 eBPF, Standalone M4 Engine.
• EVALUATED   : M4 on UNSW-NB15 (82,332 rows); M1 downshifting latency; M4 inference latency (5.72 ms).
• PLANNED     : Live M2 -> M4 HTTP dynamic query (M2 currently uses 0.12 stub); live M3 streaming;
                Multi-modal fusion (Identity, Geolocation, Device, IDS Deep Signatures into M4).
====================================================================================================</code></pre>

